WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.080
- Before the break, we were
talking about the Carter's

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.700
Show Her Love Baby
Shower I recently hosted.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.220
There were 100 new mamas and mamas-to-be

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:08.490
in the virtual celebration.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:09.490
It was so awesome,

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.800
and we actually have a few
of them joining us right now.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.000
Morgan, Amanda, Mary, are you there?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.240
Hello, everybody!

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.073
How are y'all doing?

00:00:16.073 --> 00:00:18.570
Congratulations to all of you.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.440
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.180
- So exciting!

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:25.500
Okay, so Morgan, you just
had baby Beckham, right?

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.840
So was it a difficult path
to bring him into this world?

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:28.810
I heard it was.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:29.650
- It was.

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:33.300
So I was told at 13 years
old that I had endometriosis

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.940
and that I would never have children.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.620
So by the time I met my husband,

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.090
it was like a deal-breaker for
most people that I had dated,

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.337
so I told him pretty early on like,

00:00:40.337 --> 00:00:42.600
"Hey, just so you know,
I can't have kids."

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.113
Just as casual as that, too,

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.710
and he's like, "No problem.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.730
We'll cross that bridge
when we get to it."

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.600
And literally a week
later it was Mother's Day.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.130
I went into urgent care
because I had this migraine

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.210
I couldn't get rid of, and
I found out I was pregnant.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:59.190
So (laughs) yeah, it was
kind of a funny story.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:01.750
But we were not expecting
that news at all,

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:04.650
and then between that and
six and a half years later,

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:07.730
we have had many pregnancies
that have resulted in loss

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:09.350
through miscarriage and ectopic,

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:12.160
so we tried for a really long time

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:13.670
to bring another baby into this world,

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:15.240
and like nothing went right.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.010
So I was like, I'm gonna go
ahead and get my mom makeover

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.570
and find some other things to focus on.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:21.470
And two months later,

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:23.360
I found out I was pregnant with Beckham.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:26.110
So yeah, things happen
when they're supposed to,

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:28.073
but (laughs) it's been a...

00:01:28.073 --> 00:01:28.906
- That's crazy!

00:01:28.906 --> 00:01:29.739
One of my friends was actually,

00:01:29.739 --> 00:01:31.180
the same thing happened
to her when she was young,

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.620
and they said because
of the endometriosis,

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:34.240
she wouldn't be able to have children.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.880
And she tried for years, and finally,

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.940
they were able to make it happen.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.600
She ended up having twins and it was...

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.440
That's a hard thing to hear
if your dream is to have kids,

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:46.273
you know?

00:01:46.273 --> 00:01:47.970
And that happens to a lot of women,

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:49.490
so thank you, first of
all, for being so open

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:50.830
and vulnerable about that story,

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:53.360
'cause a lot of people
connect to that story.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.040
Amanda, your pregnancy also came

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.660
as a bit of shock, right?

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:57.493
- Yeah.

00:01:57.493 --> 00:01:59.150
Actually I'm 37,

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:01.550
so I wasn't even sure
if it was still possible

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:04.440
to get pregnant or if it
was gonna be difficult,

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.960
but I went off birth control in early 2019

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.733
and we kinda just figured
whatever happens, happens.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.250
Fast forward a year and a little bit,

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:17.350
and we found out at the end
of March that I'm pregnant.

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:20.220
So that was, you know, a great news

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:23.113
and very exciting, especially
during the times of COVID.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.960
But it's made it a little
difficult, too, COVID,

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:29.600
you know, again, it's my first pregnancy,

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:31.610
so I'm not really sure what
to expect with the doctors,

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:32.750
and my husband hasn't been able

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:34.680
to come to any of my appointments.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.500
So that's been kind of difficult.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.930
He's been wanting to hear the heartbeat

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:41.330
and see the ultrasounds,
and all that fun stuff,

00:02:42.283 --> 00:02:44.280
so I've been trying to FaceTime with him

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.120
as much as possible,

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.500
but we went for our 12 week appointment,

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.925
well, I went for my 12 week appointment,

00:02:49.925 --> 00:02:52.060
and I was FaceTiming him and my parents,

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:55.740
and just so they could hear the heartbeat,

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:58.170
when the surprise, you know,
big surprise from the tech

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:00.460
was, "Oh my God, it's twins."

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.970
We didn't know that it was twins,

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:05.240
we weren't planning for twins,

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.190
it was really exciting to watch, you know,

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:09.640
both my parents and my
husband just kinda overcome

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.160
with emotion in that moment.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:12.710
- Congratulations, by the way.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:13.560
Like what a gift.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.350
And like to not know if it
was gonna happen or not,

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:17.140
and then you get two little gifts,

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:18.255
which is awesome.
- I know.

00:03:18.255 --> 00:03:19.200
- It was great.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.103
You know, you pray for a miracle
and then you get two, so.

00:03:21.103 --> 00:03:22.670
- You get two for one!

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:23.782
That's amazing!

00:03:23.782 --> 00:03:27.743
I've had two pregnancies, so
I slightly hate you. (laughs)

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.546
But no, congratulations, Amanda.

00:03:30.546 --> 00:03:32.650
That's a really, really cool story.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.830
Mary, you've had an
interesting experience as well.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:36.880
You're a nurse in an ICU.

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.320
So what's it like to
be an essential worker

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.080
who's pregnant, during a pregnancy?

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:42.860
Did you have concerns, obviously?

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:46.340
- Definitely kind of
unnerving time to be pregnant.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:47.870
Definitely unnerving time for everyone,

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:51.890
but you know, my husband and I both...

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:53.840
He works, he's a corrections
officer in a jail

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:54.800
and I'm in a hospital,

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.910
so we're both kind of in a high-risk area.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.730
So you know, just kind
of day in and day out,

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:02.480
things changing.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:05.650
My husband and I, this
is our third pregnancy,

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:10.380
first child, so you know,
we were kind of very scared

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:11.213
going into things.

00:04:11.213 --> 00:04:14.170
Thinking, well, we've had
two unsuccessful pregnancies

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:16.470
and now we have one and now
we're kind of dealing with

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:18.880
this virus that nobody
knows anything about,

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.790
and you know, I'm working in
the ICU directly with patients

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.940
who have been exposed and have the virus,

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:29.510
so it's been kind of, kinda scary.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:31.550
But you know, we have
a healthy little girl,

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:34.980
and that's three, or three
weeks away from her due date,

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:38.510
so it's very exciting, and you
know, things have been good

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:42.930
and she's been healthy this
whole process, so it's exciting.

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:45.277
I'm glad to be near the
finish line. (laughs)

00:04:45.277 --> 00:04:46.430
- Oh, oh, my gosh.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:47.680
I remember the finish line.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.668
The finish line is so beautiful.

00:04:49.668 --> 00:04:50.501
(Mary laughs)

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:51.640
It's like, oh, finally.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:55.470
I love you, get out, get
out, get out. (laughs)

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:56.303
That's really great.

00:04:56.303 --> 00:04:58.410
Hey, and thank you so much,
first of all, from all of us

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:00.630
for what you do, especially
during this time,

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:01.690
putting your life on the line.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:03.120
Not only yours, but your little baby's.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:03.953
Like that's...
- Tough.

00:05:03.953 --> 00:05:06.710
That's, it's above and beyond
to ask someone to do that,

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:08.250
so thank you so much from all of us

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.330
to just you and all the
essential workers out there.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:11.670
That's really, really...

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:12.503
- [Mary] Thank you, yeah.

00:05:12.503 --> 00:05:13.336
- Courageous of you.

00:05:13.336 --> 00:05:14.510
They already got to have an enormous

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:16.760
virtual baby shower before,

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:19.650
Huggies gifted you a year of
diapers at the Carter's Shower,

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:21.230
and they hope you'll fall
in love with the Huggies

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:22.840
special delivery diapers and wipes,

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:25.450
which are the perfect pair
for your perfect care.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:26.700
But they wanna do more.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:30.100
So they're starting a $5,000 college fund

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:33.550
for the baby of whomever wins
the game we're about to play.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:34.740
Are you ready?

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:36.084
- Yeah.

00:05:36.084 --> 00:05:36.917
- Yes.

00:05:36.917 --> 00:05:38.230
- I mean, everybody could
use money towards college.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:39.363
It is so expensive.

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:43.691
All right, let's play Baby Boom or Bust.

00:05:43.691 --> 00:05:46.910
(upbeat music)

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:48.470
Okay, so this is simple.

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:51.230
I'm gonna ask you
questions all about babies.

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:52.780
You each have cards and pens

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:53.900
right there in front of you, right?

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:55.010
You ready?

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:57.060
Okay, and when I ask the question,

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:58.720
you write your answer down.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:00.490
Then we'll see who gets it right.

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:02.080
You get it right, you get a point.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:03.980
Let's do this, all right?

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:05.710
All right, first question.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:08.351
What's the first sense a baby develops?

00:06:08.351 --> 00:06:11.240
(timer ticking)

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:13.210
Okay, are we all ready?

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:14.193
Okay, show me.

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:18.650
Okay, no one wins this one!

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:21.040
'Cause you're all wrong! (laughs)

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:23.760
The answer is actually touch.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:26.320
I didn't know that as well, so
we're all failures together.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:27.800
Okay, so let's, (laughs)

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:29.450
it's only a failure if
you don't keep trying.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:30.300
Let's keep trying.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:31.490
Okay, here we go.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:34.651
Which celebrity named their baby Stormi?

00:06:34.651 --> 00:06:38.000
(timer ticking)

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.110
All right, ladies, so
let's see the answers

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:40.943
you came up with.

00:06:40.943 --> 00:06:42.313
Let's see what you wrote.

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:45.703
Oh my God!

00:06:45.703 --> 00:06:47.310
Okay, I didn't know that at all,

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:48.940
and all of you got that right.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:50.450
Kylie Jenner is the answer.

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:52.610
Way to go, you all get points, okay.

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:54.220
I'm the loser there.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:56.030
Okay, so here's the next one.

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:58.640
What percentage of women
actually give birth

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:00.160
on their due date?

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:01.450
So here's the thing, this is hard.

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:02.900
That's like a one out of 100,

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:06.690
so I'm just gonna say whoever
gets the closest to, you know,

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:08.450
the percentage of women
actually give birth

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:10.600
on their due date, whoever gets
the closest gets the point.

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:12.630
Are y'all cool with that?

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:13.790
Okay, okay.
- Sure.

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:15.623
Here we go, show me your answer.

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:20.390
Oh my gosh!

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:21.880
One of you got the answer!

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:23.200
I had no idea, no one...

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:26.320
Okay, I cannot even believe
you right now, Mary.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.240
You got that right.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:31.740
5%! All right, so we have another one.

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:34.930
Babies are born without which body part?

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:36.349
Write down your answers.

00:07:36.349 --> 00:07:38.980
(timer ticking)

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:40.690
I think I actually did know this one,

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:42.112
'cause I thought it was weird.

00:07:42.112 --> 00:07:43.500
- [Amanda] Yes.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:44.700
- Okay, y'all ready?

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:45.750
Okay, everybody show.

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:49.090
Certain types of bones, kneecap,

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:50.303
kneecaps for the win!

00:07:51.374 --> 00:07:53.020
Amanda and Morgan get it.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:56.160
Oh my gosh, it's a three way tie!

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.830
Well, it seems like all
we can do here folks

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:02.239
is just give you all $5,000
for your babies for college.

00:08:02.239 --> 00:08:04.390
That's what we're gonna do! (laughs)

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:05.592
- That's so awesome!

00:08:05.592 --> 00:08:07.120
- That is so awesome!
- Thank you!

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:08.170
I can't believe it was
- Thank you.

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:09.090
a three way!

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:11.630
I love that, everyone wins!

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:13.930
That was so cool!

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:15.450
But literally, I'm so glad that all of you

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:16.600
ended up getting that.

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:17.760
That's courtesy of Huggies.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:18.900
Thank you so much, Huggies.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:20.860
That money is gonna go to good use.

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:23.660
And again, congratulations not
only on the five grand y'all,

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:25.160
but just on your little ones.

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:27.330
These are, they're miracle stories too,

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:28.180
you know, happening.

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:30.030
So it's a beautiful
thing to hear that hope.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:31.840
And I know a lot of mamas
out there who struggle

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:34.790
getting pregnant and
everything coming to fruition.

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:37.670
That's a hard, hard thing
to deal with emotionally

00:08:37.670 --> 00:08:38.670
and physically, mentally.

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:41.130
So thank you for being open,
thank you for being vulnerable

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:43.120
with your stories and congratulations,

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:44.540
and I just can't wait for y'all to all...

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.210
I know Beckham's born,
but the others aren't,

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:47.920
so I can't wait for y'all
to snuggle and smell 'em,

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:49.320
they're so cute.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.560
All right, y'all have a good one.

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:52.590
Stay safe and healthy, all right?

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:53.880
- [Guests] Thank you!

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:54.950
- All right, bye ladies!

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:56.060
All right, it's time for a break.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:57.655
We'll be right back with What I'm Liking.

00:08:57.655 --> 00:09:00.015
(upbeat music)

